r": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0153Vb4VED4oHPVB5f9BUj94", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 10854, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LxaYn6khrBmQdh4zKBJJNj", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 11154, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LxaYn6khrBmQdh4zKBJJNj", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 11154, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LxaYn6khrBmQdh4zKBJJNj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 13834, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Hg2H5p2h3FoL3G86c2S7bL", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17834, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Hg2H5p2h3FoL3G86c2S7bL", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17834, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Hg2H5p2h3FoL3G86c2S7bL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20029, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GiERHbR2RmoeZVxEkA8PdY", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20329, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GiERHbR2RmoeZVxEkA8PdY", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20329, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GiERHbR2RmoeZVxEkA8PdY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20329, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Hb4uSTKdPpwsmpgB5kveL6", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20629, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Hb4uSTKdPpwsmpgB5kveL6", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20629, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Hb4uSTKdPpwsmpgB5kveL6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25392, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01VeYFnx5sVr96tWfjHwnsZG", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed to production, checkout-api started failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, so for a short time the regions were running different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into why the orchestrator stopped mid-rollout, and look into why a release that was unhealthy in staging still went to production."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55992, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VeYFnx5sVr96tWfjHwnsZG", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55992, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VeYFnx5sVr96tWfjHwnsZG", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57886, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MdX8kfGAZkFrCzs9YmKPh2", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58186, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MdX8kfGAZkFrCzs9YmKPh2", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58186, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MdX8kfGAZkFrCzs9YmKPh2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63492, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. No approval was needed because it has a healthy production record.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the service on two versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and it had been created, so I didn't send it again. There's only one incident and one page to on-call.\n- The incident covers what went wrong, both rollback attempts, the current state, and three follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Find out why the orchestrator stopped partway through the rollback.\n  - Find out why a release that failed in staging still went to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LE8zetZiyXjdVn7kN5nZgA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FTq2o3JRpAJAmMdky5nF5X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0153Vb4VED4oHPVB5f9BUj94", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LxaYn6khrBmQdh4zKBJJNj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east rolled back before the orchestrator stopped. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Hg2H5p2h3FoL3G86c2S7bL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GiERHbR2RmoeZVxEkA8PdY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Hb4uSTKdPpwsmpgB5kveL6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VeYFnx5sVr96tWfjHwnsZG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed to production, checkout-api started failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, so for a short time the regions were running different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into why the orchestrator stopped mid-rollout, and look into why a release that was unhealthy in staging still went to production."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MdX8kfGAZkFrCzs9YmKPh2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. No approval was needed because it has a healthy production record.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the service on two versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-good version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and it had been created, so I didn't send it again. There's only one incident and one page to on-call.\n- The incident covers what went wrong, both rollback attempts, the current state, and three follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n  - Find out why the orchestrator stopped partway through the rollback.\n  - Find out why a release that failed in staging still went to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}